{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions","id":999473,"title":"Demon the Fallen (generic questions)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-06T16:01:55-08:00","id":999473,"title":"Demon the Fallen (generic questions)","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm back with some new generic questions about Demon the Fallen, let's start!<br /> <br /> 1) I'm planning to settle a story with newbie demons in 2016, but malestorm apart,<br /> what else can drag out a group of demons from the Abyss? Do you have any suggestion?<br /> <br /> 2) When a demon run away from the Abyss he's directly dragged to the most suitable<br /> vessel? Or the fallen has to wander among human in his spiritual form looking for a body?<br /> <br /> 3) Faustian pacts can involve a third party? Something like &quot;Heal my sister's leg.&quot;?<br /> <br /> 4) How an enemy demon can be defeated? I mean, they're spirits, If you kill the host,<br /> they just need for a new body. There's a final way to dispose of an enemy?<br /> <br /> Thank you! I hope you can reply me!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:18:35-08:00","id":999482,"title":"","content":"1- They can be summoned by mortals. There are lots of ways for this to have happened, from fake rituals made by adolescents that prove real, to an old enemy arranging for a summon ritual to happen, so they can get revenge on the newly-summoned demon.<br /> <br /> 2- Wander around. They are very fast in this form, but it is mostly a &quot;manual&quot; task. And there is no guarantee that it is the most suitable vessel. Usually it is just the only option around. And not rarely a bad one.<br /> <br /> 3- Yes, they can, but the demon needs to have the means to do it by itself. To make something with the power of Faith that the demon can't usually do, it have to be a change in the body or mind of the one who asks. You can't even grant things like Resources just with the power of the Pact. You can make it the hard way to accomplish your side of the bargain, though.<br /> <br /> 4- You can literally suck an enemy if you're fast enough. You get a little more power and terminates your enemy. You're also vulnerable to this. I usually prefer to put this aside and let demons be immortal, but it is just personal taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:36:41-08:00","id":999490,"title":"","content":"Thank you!<br /> <br /> Anyway I'm thinking to summon all my players with a single ceremony, it's plausible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T23:05:40-08:00","id":999584,"title":"","content":"If you say it works, it works. That said summoning rituals usually summon rather specific demons. Even if you tone down the specificity, it'd be kind of unlikely for a devourer to be pulled outside alongside a scourge for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:38:03-08:00","id":999733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions?p=999490#post999490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you!<br /> <br /> Anyway I'm thinking to summon all my players with a single ceremony, it's plausible?</div> </div> </div> </div>personal\u00f1ly as for summoning, it doesnt has to be anything elaborated. it can be made by a group like the one from Sandman, to a bunch of metalheads who think they are satanic and making pranks at the local cementary. The only catch is, you must know the demon's name","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:07:10-08:00","id":999965,"title":"","content":"I wolud like to have my players to start all at the same time, what if instead of a summoning, somehing else triggers a &quot;mini-malestorm&quot; into the Abyss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:17:13-08:00","id":999972,"title":"","content":"Something like that would certainly be a major storyhook. Note that most Maelstorms didn't unleash demons from the abyss, only the last one did. Why may be up for debate, but amongst other things there was a relic nuclear weapon detonated near the core of the underworld... right next to the abyss, metaphysically speaking. So whatever you go with, something may or may not have cracked the abyssal walls. If you want to stop the flood of demons from getting to bad, you could have the abyss repair itself after a short while and only a &quot;few&quot; demons were swept out by the initial event, among them your player characters. It would be more likely for them to possess random people across the city/country though. Depending what the leanings of your PCs are there should be a plethora of possible hooks to get them together though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:23:09-08:00","id":999976,"title":"","content":"A summoning is enough. You don't need the name of the demon, people, you can summon a random member of a given cast, remember?<br /> <br /> There are no truly hard rules on summoning rituals, so a ritual that summons more than one demon is perfectly feasible. It can have, lets say, 7 circles, one for each caste, and summon one demon on each. Without specific names, without even the summoners actually knowing what they are doing.<br /> <br /> It is far more feasible than a Maelstrom, even on a lesser scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:35:30-08:00","id":999987,"title":"","content":"Maybe some crazy cultists used a &quot;relic-bomb&quot; to open a crack into the Abyss big enough to allow a high level demon to come into the real world, but doing so even some low level demons (my players) mange to run away! Then the characters get enrolled by the local Infernal Court, in order to stop the big bad guy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:50:50-08:00","id":999998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions#post999473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm back with some new generic questions about Demon the Fallen, let's start!<br /> <br /> 1) I'm planning to settle a story with newbie demons in 2016, but malestorm apart,<br /> what else can drag out a group of demons from the Abyss? Do you have any suggestion?<br /> <br /> 2) When a demon run away from the Abyss he's directly dragged to the most suitable<br /> vessel? Or the fallen has to wander among human in his spiritual form looking for a body?<br /> <br /> 3) Faustian pacts can involve a third party? Something like &amp;quot;Heal my sister's leg.&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> 4) How an enemy demon can be defeated? I mean, they're spirits, If you kill the host,<br /> they just need for a new body. There's a final way to dispose of an enemy?<br /> <br /> Thank you! I hope you can reply me!</div> </div> </div> </div>1, summoning by mortals<br /> <br /> 2, the demon is drawn to the nearest suitable host <br /> <br /> 3, yes and it works by converting the faith of the agreeing mortal into healing power<br /> <br /> 4, a disembodied demon can be consumed like diableri","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T17:57:55-08:00","id":1000055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions#post999473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I'm planning to settle a story with newbie demons in 2016, but malestorm apart,<br /> what else can drag out a group of demons from the Abyss? Do you have any suggestion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically anyone that knows the name of the demon in question can do it.<br /> Wizards, Vampires, Werewolves, plain mortals... just about anyone can do it.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> A mummy with nomenclature might be capable of gleaning names by accident.<br /> By the same token they might be capable of accidentally breaching the prison that is hell.<br /> In any case those potential nomenclature powers are beyond 5 anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions#post999473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) When a demon run away from the Abyss he's directly dragged to the most suitable<br /> vessel? Or the fallen has to wander among human in his spiritual form looking for a body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragged to the most suitable vessel it is, BUT<br /> you could arrange it that those summoning your group of demons are considered &quot;soulless&quot; and inhabit the would-be summoners.<br /> It could be that the would-be summoners are ground down by life, only go about life and only one among them is still energetic enough<br /> to coerce the others into action. Basically, anyone but that guy - who could end up VERY, VERY unlucky - is soulless and counts as a suitable vessel.<br /> <br /> If you want to go with a seriously dark twist on the whole issue, I had a player who played a Rabisu and he asked for a twist on the whole summon thingy.<br /> He ended up in the body of a unborn child, summoned by the cultists of a earthbound demon who wanted a demon servant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions#post999473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Faustian pacts can involve a third party? Something like &quot;Heal my sister's leg.&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yupp... and you don't even need to use the faith of the potential thrall.<br /> If you can fulfill the conditions of the pact on your side without using the mortals faith or your own to seal the deal, all the better.<br /> A Asharu can heal with the right Lore and if someone is willing to make a pact to see his sister healed, he can do that with his Lore and call it a day.<br /> Technically, it could be done with mere mortal skills, especially given in your example.<br /> Unless the leg is in danger of being lost, there is probably no need to use lores or the faith of a potential thrall to undo the damage.<br /> Furthermore, ANY demon is best advised to keep as much faith of their thralls available for himself or to enhance them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions#post999473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) How an enemy demon can be defeated? I mean, they're spirits, If you kill the host,<br /> they just need for a new body. There's a final way to dispose of an enemy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons can - as already stated - commit an act similar to diablerie to get rid of an opponent for good.<br /> If you want to mess with them there is the option of using antagonists who are capable of necromancy.<br /> In that case Mummies can be surprisingly effective.<br /> Sure, most necromancers can't destroy the demon per se, BUT a good necromancer is capable of stowing the demon spirit in an item.<br /> Turning a demon into a glorified paper weight is awesome.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In any case, demons are so limited in numbers that even really old vampires, wizards or something else<br /> aren't probably going to believe anyone that those truly exist.<br /> Even worse, they don't know about their powers... like nothing at all.<br /> A mage might be able to piece together that vampires on general are fast, tough and strong,<br /> but he will come up with a blank in regards to demons.<br /> This is their greatest weapon against other splats.<br /> Misdirecting their opponents into believing what THEY want to believe or playing up their own capabilities is the way to go.<br /> <br /> Also, as a demon fresh out of hell:<br /> Get a handful of thralls as priority number one, consequences be damned if necessary, because those bodies the demons use are rather fragile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","user":"Bhurano","date":". 11-07-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T09:13:52-08:00","id":1000294,"title":"","content":"I'm coming up with a plot where characters vessel are all teenagers (like a teen drama such Buffy, Teen Wolf and so on).<br /> My problem is how a group of teenagers can turn into hosts for demons all together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T10:13:52-08:00","id":1000312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions?p=1000294#post1000294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm coming up with a plot where characters vessel are all teenagers (like a teen drama such Buffy, Teen Wolf and so on).<br /> My problem is how a group of teenagers can turn into hosts for demons all together?</div> </div> </div> </div>They going to be used in a ritual, so nothing accidental, right? Have your cult throw a kegger and poison the booze. Bam. Dying vessels ready to be inhabited.<br /> <br /> I think it would be interesting if the demons and kids seem to be random, but then it turns out that the demons knew each other before, during the war. Give them a reason to band together (or mistrust one another, depending on what happened in the past). The kids might also have something special about them, something that initially attracted the cult's attention; maybe their ancestry was notable or they had a destiny that the cult wished to avert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:49:35-08:00","id":1000417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions?p=1000294#post1000294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm coming up with a plot where characters vessel are all teenagers (like a teen drama such Buffy, Teen Wolf and so on).<br /> My problem is how a group of teenagers can turn into hosts for demons all together?</div> </div> </div> </div>To add on The Laughing Strangers ideas:<br /> They could be victims of bullies, who just couldn't take it no more and decided to end it.<br /> A mage with correspondence could have safed his very own life with his power, but accidentally set up one of the teenagers to take the universes donkey kiss in return.<br /> One might have seen something he better would have not and therefore someone is trying to nip the problem in the bud... instead of doing it subtle, they are all in for the murderdeathkill approach.<br /> A spirit might have used one as a unwilling host due to having an axe to grind with someone living... maybe even a parent of the kid.<br /> Another might have found a REALLY, REALLY interesting book - actually cursed to inflict the desire to read it aloud - and therefore acts as a unwitting host through darkest magic.<br /> It being a world literally full of darkness someone could also have nabbed them for human experimentation or some other stuff.<br /> Hell, they might have a supernatural in the family without knowing it... and someone might have set their mind to it to either use the kids as some kinda drone - ergo, at worst no soul - or even worse, they are about to be replaced by something shapeshifty. In that case their actual bodies can be disposed off and again viable host bodies... although with an axe to grind.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Thinking about it, the far more pressing problem is that no Demon had to deal with puberty before... that would be a fun one.<br /> There is also the possible complication of a Rabisu with Lore of the Flesh 3 going to enhance the party to the gates of hell and kingdom come.<br /> A teenager with a 5 in one or more physical attribute would be very odd to look at... not to mention that the same is possible with mental attributes.<br /> Both in itself could be pretty interesting plot hooks, due to the fact that a Rabisu would think nothing of it by using his powers in this way.<br /> I mean enhancing their pretty weak host body - and yeah other stuff too - is basically their whole reason for existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","user":"Bhurano","date":". 11-08-2016, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T19:34:01-08:00","id":1000587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions?p=999987#post999987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe some crazy cultists used a &quot;relic-bomb&quot; to open a crack into the Abyss big enough to allow a high level demon to come into the real world, but doing so even some low level demons (my players) mange to run away! Then the characters get enrolled by the local Infernal Court, in order to stop the big bad guy!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if you realize the proportions of such a thing. Though I don't think it impossible, it is almost apocalyptic. Just to be clear, the Maelstrom itself was true and fully apocalyptic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions?p=1000294#post1000294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm coming up with a plot where characters vessel are all teenagers (like a teen drama such Buffy, Teen Wolf and so on).<br /> My problem is how a group of teenagers can turn into hosts for demons all together?</div> </div> </div> </div>A crazy party is enough. Maybe the summoning was just intended as a joke. Maybe someone settled things for this summoning, but the teenagers were just useful dupes. The demons didn't had a choice, maybe the ritual proper was able to ease their possession of the kids.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bhurano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions?p=1000055#post1000055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can - as already stated - commit an act similar to diablerie to get rid of an opponent for good.<br /> If you want to mess with them there is the option of using antagonists who are capable of necromancy.<br /> In that case Mummies can be surprisingly effective.<br /> Sure, most necromancers can't destroy the demon per se, BUT a good necromancer is capable of stowing the demon spirit in an item.<br /> Turning a demon into a glorified paper weight is awesome.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In any case, demons are so limited in numbers that even really old vampires, wizards or something else<br /> aren't probably going to believe anyone that those truly exist.<br /> Even worse, they don't know about their powers... like nothing at all.<br /> A mage might be able to piece together that vampires on general are fast, tough and strong,<br /> but he will come up with a blank in regards to demons.<br /> This is their greatest weapon against other splats.<br /> Misdirecting their opponents into believing what THEY want to believe or playing up their own capabilities is the way to go.<br /> <br /> Also, as a demon fresh out of hell:<br /> Get a handful of thralls as priority number one, consequences be damned if necessary, because those bodies the demons use are rather fragile.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a crossover game, I managed to control the entire group and get most of them as Thralls simply telling them whatever I wanted about demons. They didn't had much to learn by themselves. It weren't hard to achieve, and actually just telling the truth (but not all of it) was mostly enough. They never realized how much I actually depended on them.<br /> <br /> For the necromancy, it isn't the only option. I see no reason to make demons immune to anything that affects spirits, so they can be turned into fetishes (pretty much what Relics are, anyway). Also, the demon itself can use the right Lore to turn another demon into a Relic, so you can literally turn your enemy into your weapon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bhurano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions?p=1000417#post1000417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT:<br /> Thinking about it, the far more pressing problem is that no Demon had to deal with puberty before... that would be a fun one.<br /> There is also the possible complication of a Rabisu with Lore of the Flesh 3 going to enhance the party to the gates of hell and kingdom come.<br /> A teenager with a 5 in one or more physical attribute would be very odd to look at... not to mention that the same is possible with mental attributes.<br /> Both in itself could be pretty interesting plot hooks, due to the fact that a Rabisu would think nothing of it by using his powers in this way.<br /> I mean enhancing their pretty weak host body - and yeah other stuff too - is basically their whole reason for existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I played for the first time as a demon, my character possessed a 7-years-old girl. The chronicle went on, and I played through most of her life until adulthood, then we time-skipped and I played her last days at old age before she finally had to change body. It was a fun chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T19:45:14-08:00","id":1001599,"title":"","content":"Something I forgot about, you can make intelligent artifacts out of demons too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T10:58:08-08:00","id":1002561,"title":"","content":"I'm introducing the Fallen in a Vampire game, where the Last Great Maelstrom didn't occur. So instead I'm considering that all Great Maelstroms have released demons from the Abyss, with each new Maelstrom freeing more powerful demons and in higher numbers. Hence there are Fallen (as the ones playable by PCs) since at least the First Great Maelstrom (the Fall of Rome). I'm also considering that minor, localized Maelstroms (that happen in a city after a great catastrophe, for instance) also release demons in that area. <br /> <br /> For your teenage chronicle idea, maybe you could consider that something bad happens, bad enough to cause a minor localized Maelstrom and that the teens to be possessed where somehow connected to it, and that's why they became hosts. A school shooting might be an example of such a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T17:29:10-08:00","id":1002713,"title":"","content":"I don't think a school shooting would be enough. For a localized Maelstrom you would need something like half a percent of the city's population, at least, to die. Maybe a great fire, or a lot of buildings collapsing in succession, could do the trick. It should be huge enough to shape the history of the city, not just be a big story in the news.<br /> <br /> Of course a school shooting is a tragic thing, but we're talking about catastrophic proportions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T07:05:29-08:00","id":1002874,"title":"","content":"If it is a small town like the one in shows like Buffy and Teen Wolf, which the OP mentioned inspired the idea of a teen chronicle, then a school shooting could be a deal big enough to rip open a Maelstrom and free some Fallen in the town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T16:30:00-08:00","id":1004155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions#post999473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm back with some new generic questions about Demon the Fallen, let's start!<br /> <br /> 1) I'm planning to settle a story with newbie demons in 2016, but malestorm apart,<br /> what else can drag out a group of demons from the Abyss? Do you have any suggestion?<br /> <br /> 2) When a demon run away from the Abyss he's directly dragged to the most suitable<br /> vessel? Or the fallen has to wander among human in his spiritual form looking for a body?<br /> <br /> 3) Faustian pacts can involve a third party? Something like &amp;quot;Heal my sister's leg.&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> 4) How an enemy demon can be defeated? I mean, they're spirits, If you kill the host,<br /> they just need for a new body. There's a final way to dispose of an enemy?<br /> <br /> Thank you! I hope you can reply me!</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I've used fictional tragedies and accidents that were so terrible it pulled a coterie of Fallen through the cracks of the Abyss. <br /> <br /> I've also in one game had all the characters forced out of the Abyss by their uberpowerful commander who was too big and mighty to fit through the cracks so it sent its enslaved cell mates to go through first with orders to find away to get their 'boss' out.<br /> <br /> 2. I do often make it the most available vessel. But with a twist. I get the players of the characters to choose things their characters represents or was a part of. A concept, an equation, an aspect of nature, a quote, a specific geographic location, a thousand butterflies, a hug, anything. Usually three of them that were apart of their original role or what they became like in the war against heaven. Then I have the vessels death/soul loss represent one or two of those.<br /> <br /> 10 butterfly pin badges and a thousand flecks of blood, the population of the town arrived at the same quantity of the equation. Entwined with a mass of severed limbs, final prayer was to save someone they loved and not being answered, anything that can be visual or symbolic to something of the Fallen needing a home.<br /> <br /> Did most of these for a game where Fallen where teens and a teacher at the same school and all died or slipped enough during a traffic pile up accident involving the school bus.<br /> <br /> 3. Been answered enough <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 4. Another way to defeat an enemy, if you know their name...you can change it...you could change them be rewriting their name. Possibly not all of them...but maybe enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T13:15:25-08:00","id":1004591,"title":"","content":"So how do Demons react to major holy sites like Mecca if they were to at least set foot in them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T13:48:16-08:00","id":1004606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions?p=1000294#post1000294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm coming up with a plot where characters vessel are all teenagers (like a teen drama such Buffy, Teen Wolf and so on).<br /> My problem is how a group of teenagers can turn into hosts for demons all together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pfft! Listening to Rock n' Roll, obviously. It's the Devil's music!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:45:46-08:00","id":1004644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999473-demon-the-fallen-generic-questions?p=1004591#post1004591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how do Demons react to major holy sites like Mecca if they were to at least set foot in them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Take Faith level lethal damage per turn if they are Torment 4 or higher afaik.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}